The basics are pretty straightforward, though occasionally complex (converting 
internal connectives into external ones, shifting quantifiers to the front and 
figuring out their scopes).  The more interesting problems involve stripping off 
the human elements: questions (though those can be made to fit logic), 
exclamations, commands and the like.  I don't know of anyone who has tried to 
write a program for doing all (or any) of this, but it seems perfectly feasible 
-- though not, perhaps, in a master''s degree time frame.



